{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA COMPLETE — disposition: ACCEPTED (host-environment artifact, no code fix warranted).\n\nRoot cause: the injected Copilot/Git environment sets GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=3 with KEY_0=safe.bareRepository=explicit (also credential.interactive=never, core.fsmonitor=\"\"). The test helper reads the bare fixture remotes via `git -C <tickets-remote.git> ...`; with safe.bareRepository=explicit git REFUSES to operate on a bare repo discovered via -C, yielding exit 128 (the refs/heads/tickets ref actually exists). Not git 2.55.0 behavior, not origin/main breakage.\n\nProof: with the injected GIT_CONFIG_* removed, the same host+git gives `17 passed`. Neutralizing just the one key also fixes it:\n  env GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=4 GIT_CONFIG_KEY_3=safe.bareRepository GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_3=all PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test  → 17 passed\n\nCI impact: NONE. Gerrit `Verified` runs on ubuntu-latest without this injected env, so the cluster is green in CI.\n\nGuidance for the janitor epic (78f2): full-suite LOCAL pre-flight on this host must prepend the safe.bareRepository=all override (append as GIT_CONFIG entry #3). This does NOT block landing. No production/test code change required."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788474946289117332,"uuid":"43e8e59a-2c79-467d-ac37-4740caa86c5f"}